Appendix D: Bayes Risk Exposure Fraction

D.1 Definition and range

Let

R_H^* = \inf_{d_H: \mathcal{H} \to \mathcal{D}} \mathbb{E}[L(d_H(h), \Theta)],

R_{\text{joint}}^* = \inf_{d: \mathcal{H} \times \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{D}} \mathbb{E}[L(d(h, E), \Theta)],

R_\delta = \mathbb{E}[L(\delta(h, E), \Theta)].

Define

\alpha_{\text{BR}} = \frac{R_H^* - R_\delta}{R_H^* - R_{\text{joint}}^*}.

Claim. If R_{\text{joint}}^* \le R_\delta \le R_H^*, then \alpha_{\text{BR}} \in [0,1].

Proof. The denominator is non-negative because \mathcal{H} \times \mathcal{E} contains \mathcal{H} as a coordinate subspace, so the joint infimum cannot exceed the human-only infimum. The numerator is non-negative because R_\delta \le R_H^*, and non-greater than the denominator because R_\delta \ge R_{\text{joint}}^*. Therefore \alpha_{\text{BR}} \in [0,1]. \blacksquare

D.2 Interpretation regimes

· \alpha_{\text{BR}} = 0 \iff R_\delta = R_H^*: agents contribute zero risk reduction.
· \alpha_{\text{BR}} = 1 \iff R_\delta = R_{\text{joint}}^*: agents contribute the maximum achievable reduction.
· \alpha_{\text{BR}} < 0 \iff R_\delta > R_H^*: deference strictly degrades performance.

D.3 Quadratic loss in the linear-Gaussian model

Let L(d, \Theta) = (d - \Theta)^2. The Bayes-optimal human-only rule is the posterior mean \mathbb{E}[\Theta \mid h], with risk

R_H^* = \frac{\sigma_\Theta^2 \tau^2}{\sigma_\Theta^2 + \tau^2}.

The Bayes-optimal joint rule is \mathbb{E}[\Theta \mid h, E], with posterior precision

\frac{1}{\sigma_{\text{post}}^2} = \frac{1}{\sigma_\Theta^2} + \frac{1}{\tau^2} + \frac{n_{\text{eff}}}{\sigma^2},

so

R_{\text{joint}}^* = \frac{1}{\sigma_\Theta^{-2} + \tau^{-2} + n_{\text{eff}} \sigma^{-2}}.

For the linear rule D = (1-\lambda)h + \lambda \bar{e}, the risk is R_\delta = V as in Appendix A. The exposure fraction \alpha_{\text{BR}} then interpolates between the human-only and joint-optimal baselines in a manner consistent with the variance-share exposure \alpha, though the two coincide exactly only when \lambda is chosen to minimize V.

