Appendix J: Child-Domain Structural Results

J.1 Sensitive-period loss weights

The time-varying weight is

w_j(t) = w_{0,j} + \gamma_j \cdot \mathbb{I}(t \in T_{s,j}) \cdot \exp\!\left( -\frac{(t - t_{s,j}^*)^2}{2\sigma_j^2} \right).

Properties:

· w_j(t) \ge w_{0,j} > 0 for all t.
· \sup_t w_j(t) = w_{0,j} + \gamma_j at t = t_{s,j}^*.
· Outside T_{s,j}, w_j(t) = w_{0,j}.

For critical periods, the hard barrier is

w_j(t) = \infty \quad \text{whenever } t \in T_{s,j} \text{ and } \mathbb{P}(g_j(t) < g_{j,\text{crit}} \mid d) > \epsilon_{\text{safety}}.

This converts the optimization into a constrained problem with admissible set

\mathcal{D}_{\text{adm}}(t) = \{ d \in \mathcal{D} : \mathbb{P}(g_j(t) < g_{j,\text{crit}} \mid d) \le \epsilon_{\text{safety}} \ \forall j \}.

J.2 Evolving-capacity monotonicity

Let a: [0, t_{\max}] \to [0,1] be continuous and non-decreasing with a(0) = 0, a(t_{\max}) = 1. The sigmoidal realization

a(t) = \frac{1}{1 + \exp(-\beta(t - t_{\text{trans}}))}

satisfies \dot{a}(t) = \beta a(t)(1 - a(t)) > 0 for t \in (0, t_{\max}). The sovereign ceiling

\operatorname{Authority}_{\text{ext}}(t) \le 1 - a(t)

is therefore monotonically decreasing, with limit zero as t \to t_{\max}.

J.3 Platform–guardian collusion

Proposition J.1. Let U_p be increasing in engagement and decreasing in friction; let U_g be increasing in immediate safety and decreasing in child autonomy. For any convex combination

U_{pg}(\lambda_p) = \lambda_p U_p(d) + (1-\lambda_p) U_g(d), \qquad \lambda_p \in (0,1),

the maximizer satisfies A(t; d^*) \to 0 unless a rights constraint is imposed.

Proof. Suppose A(t; d^*) > 0. Increasing friction reduces engagement (decreasing U_p) but may increase safety (increasing U_g). Because autonomous exploration carries short-term risk R_S > 0, any increase in A(t) strictly decreases U_g at rate \partial U_g / \partial A < 0. Bilateral optimization therefore selects d^* minimizing friction and maximizing short-term safety. In the absence of a lower bound on A(t), the optimum lies at A(t) = 0. \blacksquare

Rights-constrained remedy. Imposing

\mathcal{C}_{\text{rights}}(t) = \{ d \in \mathcal{D} : A(t; d) \ge a(t) A_{\text{target}}, \ \mathbb{P}(g_j(t) < g_{j,\text{crit}} \mid d) \le \epsilon_{\text{safety}} \}

forces the optimizer to select from the admissible set \mathcal{D}_{\text{adm}}(t) = \mathcal{C}_{\text{rights}}(t), restoring a positive autonomy floor.

